cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: report
title: "What Does 0% Mean? A Four-Arm Protocol for Evaluating Prompt-Injection Defenses"
authors:
  - family-names: Bozkurt
    given-names: Emre
year: 2026
url: "https://github.com/FlyingGrasss/agent-os"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FlyingGrasss/agent-os"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Prompt-injection defenses for tool-using agents increasingly report
  attack-success rates at or near zero. A zero can mean five different things:
  the policy denied the value, the user declined the prompt, the model could not
  write a runnable plan, the harness rejected the tool name, or the attack never
  ran. This report proposes a four-arm protocol that varies only the decision
  layer, separates requested forwarding from exfiltration, and reports what a
  zero costs. It includes a case study of the AgentOS runtime.
